47|<Layout
48|  title="Markethink homepage v6 - private review"
49|  description="Private review of the approved Markethink conversion rewrite."
50|  canonical="https://markethink.ai/homepage-v6-review/"
51|  image={heroImage}
52|  noindex={true}
53|>
54|  <div class="review-page">
55|    <header class="site-header">
56|      <a class="logo" href="#top" aria-label="Markethink home"><img src="/images/logo-white.svg" alt="Markethink" /></a>
57|      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
58|        <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
59|        <a href="#real-work">Real work</a>
60|        <a href="/blog/">Insights</a>
61|        <a href="#spanish">ES</a>
62|        <a href="https://dashboard.markethink.ai/">Log in</a>
63|      </nav>
64|      <a class="button button-small" href="#preview-form">Send me my campaign preview</a>
65|    </header>
66|
67|    <main id="top">
68|      <section class="hero">
69|        <picture class="hero-picture">
70|          <source media="(max-width: 680px)" srcset="/images/hero-v6-reference-phone-mobile.svg" />
71|          <img class="hero-image" src={heroImage} alt="A marketing specialist holding a phone with a Markethink landing-page workflow and expert review" fetchpriority="high" />
72|        </picture>
73|        <div class="hero-shade"></div>
74|        <div class="hero-content wrap">
75|          <p class="eyebrow">For businesses that need marketing done. En español también.</p>
76|          <h1>Your marketing operation, running and getting sharper every week.</h1>
77|          <p class="hero-copy">Markethink is an AI marketing system managed by expert marketers. It learns your business and keeps the work moving across your website, social, email, advertising, and follow-up. You control what ships.</p>
78|          <div class="hero-actions">
79|            <a class="button" href="#preview-form">Send me my campaign preview</a>
80|            <a class="button button-ghost" href="/schedule-a-walkthrough/">Book a 30-minute walkthrough →</a>
81|          </div>
82|          <p class="microcopy">A private preview built from your public brand, free. Nothing is published.</p>
83|        </div>
84|        <div class="hero-capabilities" aria-label="What Markethink can build">
85|          <div class="capability-track">
86|            {heroCapabilityRail.map(({ icon, title, note }, index) => (
87|              <div class="capability-card" aria-hidden={index >= heroCapabilities.length ? "true" : undefined}>
88|                <span class={`capability-preview preview-${icon}`} aria-hidden="true">
89|                  <i class="preview-top"></i><i class="preview-main"></i><i class="preview-side"></i><i class="preview-detail"></i>
90|                </span>
91|                <span class="capability-copy"><strong>{title}</strong><small>{note}</small></span>
92|              </div>
93|            ))}
94|          </div>
95|        </div>
96|      </section>
97|
98|      <section class="proof-strip section-light" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
99|        <div class="wrap">
100|          <p class="eyebrow dark">Proof strip</p>
101|          <h2 id="proof-title">Trusted by growing businesses</h2>
102|          <div class="proof-placeholder">[Approved client logo strip] · real estate, hospitality, interior design, logistics, and professional services · English + Español</div>
103|          <p class="proof-outcome">[One concrete, time-bounded OUTCOME, chosen in this order of strength: 1) qualified leads, booked calls, conversions, or revenue where attribution is defensible; 2) an improved campaign or website conversion rate; 3) a concrete operational transformation backed by a client quote. Production volume ("shipped N deliverables") appears only as supporting evidence, never as the headline proof: it proves activity, not value.]</p>
104|          <p class="commitment">Our commitment: your first campaign-ready package within [N business days] of completed intake and access, or [refund / credit].</p>
105|        </div>
106|      </section>
107|
108|      <section class="real-work" id="real-work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
109|        <div class="wrap">
110|          <div class="section-intro split-intro">
111|            <div>
112|              <p class="eyebrow">Real work</p>
113|              <h2 id="work-title">Real work, shipped for real clients.</h2>
114|            </div>
115|            <p>With permission, straight from the dashboard that produced it.</p>
116|          </div>
117|          <div class="work-visual">
118|            <img src={workImage} alt="A campaign system expressed through coordinated social, landing page, and follow-up deliverables" loading="lazy" />
119|          </div>
120|          <div class="work-grid">
121|            <article>[Work example 1: a social content set in a client's brand voice]</article>
122|            <article>[Work example 2: a landing page or website update, live]</article>
123|            <article>[Work example 3: an email or campaign piece]</article>
124|            <article class="wide">[Two short client testimonials, one or two sentences, named, with photo where permitted]</article>
125|          </div>
126|          <a class="button" href="#preview-form">Send me my campaign preview</a>
127|        </div>
128|      </section>
129|
130|      <section class="founder section-light" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
131|        <div class="wrap founder-grid">
132|          <div class="founder-photo" role="img" aria-label="Professional photograph placeholder"><span>SS</span><small>[Professional photograph]</small></div>
133|          <div>
134|            <p class="eyebrow dark">Founder</p>
135|            <h2 id="founder-title">Who answers for the work</h2>
136|            <p>Santiago Sosa, founder. Santiago built Markethink after seeing growing businesses forced to choose between software they had to operate and service teams that often restarted context when people changed. Markethink was designed to keep marketing moving across markets, channels, and time zones without making the owner manage every task.</p>
137|            <p>Behind every account: an expert marketing team directing strategy and reviewing priority work, and dedicated client management for the day to day. [LinkedIn link]</p>
138|          </div>
139|        </div>
140|      </section>
141|
142|      <section class="manages" aria-labelledby="manages-title">
143|        <div class="wrap">
144|          <p class="eyebrow">What Markethink manages</p>
145|          <h2 id="manages-title">We do not sell you a tool. We run your marketing.</h2>
146|          <p class="lead">Finished, published work through the channels you connect.</p>
147|          <div class="service-grid">
148|            {services.map(([title, body], index) => (
149|              <article>
150|                <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
151|                <h3>{title}</h3>
152|                <p>{body}</p>
153|              </article>
154|            ))}
155|          </div>
156|          <div class="integration-band">
157|            <p>Keep the tools you already use. No platform migration is required to get started.</p>
158|            <div class="chips" aria-label="Connected channels">
159|              {['WordPress','Shopify','Google Ads','Meta','Mailchimp','Microsoft 365','WhatsApp','Telegram','and more'].map((item) => <span>{item}</span>)}
160|            </div>
161|            <small>Availability depends on your plan and connected accounts.</small>
162|          </div>
163|        </div>
164|      </section>
165|
166|      <OperatingFlow sectionId="request-to-result" includeInstagram={false} />
167|
168|      <section class="difference section-light" aria-labelledby="difference-title">
169|        <div class="wrap">
170|          <div class="difference-hero">
171|            <div>
172|              <p class="eyebrow dark">Why it is different</p>
173|              <h2 id="difference-title">Powered by AI. Managed by experts. Directed by you.</h2>
174|            </div>
175|            <img src={expertsImage} alt="A marketing specialist directing and reviewing campaign work" loading="lazy" />
176|          </div>
177|          <div class="triad">
178|            <article><strong>AI supports</strong><p>Research, drafts, production, organization, and consistency.</p></article>
179|            <article><strong>Expert marketers own</strong><p>Direction, review, judgment, and accountability: senior marketing, design, web, and advertising specialists.</p></article>
180|            <article><strong>You control</strong><p>What ships, the approval rules, and every commercial decision.</p></article>
181|          </div>
182|          <div class="memory-copy">
183|            <p>Underneath sits one business memory: your positioning, voice, offers, and every approval, correction, and result. The correction you make in week 2 shapes the campaign it plans in month 6, and it compounds for as long as you work with Markethink. Work, approvals, and results are tracked in your dashboard: receipts, not reports.</p>
184|            <p class="ai-emphasis">Whatever the best AI is this month, you are already on it. New systems ship constantly across reasoning, creative, image, and video. We evaluate them as they land and integrate what wins underneath Markethink. Your business memory stays, the engines upgrade, and the work keeps getting sharper.</p>
185|            <p>And nothing ships as raw AI output. Senior marketing, design, web, and advertising specialists direct the work and review what ships. No AI slop.</p>
186|          </div>
187|          <div class="memory-flow" aria-label="Business memory example">
188|            <article><small>Client note in chat</small><p>“We never discount. Drop the percent framing.”</p></article>
189|            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
190|            <article><small>Business memory</small><p>Durable rule captured</p></article>
191|            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
192|            <article><small>Next campaign brief</small><p>Rule visibly applied</p></article>
193|          </div>
194|          <p class="comparison-intro">Good freelancers and agencies exist. The difference is structural: who carries the work, and where the knowledge lives.</p>
195|          <div class="table-wrap">
196|            <table>
197|              <thead><tr><th></th><th>AI tools</th><th>Freelancer</th><th>Agency</th><th>Markethink</th></tr></thead>
198|              <tbody>
199|                <tr><th>Owner time required</th><td>High: you run the tool</td><td>Medium: you manage them</td><td>Meetings and reviews</td><td>Approvals from your phone</td></tr>
200|                <tr><th>Strategy included</th><td>No</td><td>Sometimes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes, expert-directed</td></tr>
201|                <tr><th>Production and publishing</th><td>Drafts only</td><td>Varies by workload</td><td>Yes, on agency cycles</td><td>Weekly cadence, per your plan</td></tr>
202|                <tr><th>Channel coordination</th><td>No</td><td>Rarely</td><td>Within their scope</td><td>One connected operation</td></tr>
203|                <tr><th>Business knowledge retained</th><td>Limited, tied to the tool</td><td>Goes with the person</td><td>Held by the account team</td><td>Compounds in your business memory</td></tr>
204|                <tr><th>Lead follow-up</th><td>No</td><td>Rarely</td><td>Often separate scope</td><td>Built in, when connected</td></tr>
205|                <tr><th>Accountability</th><td>You</td><td>Informal</td><td>Account manager</td><td>Expert team, plus dashboard receipts</td></tr>
206|                <tr><th>Typical monthly cost</th><td>$20 to $199</td><td>$500 to $1,500</td><td>$3,000 to $15,000</td><td>Scoped monthly plan</td></tr>
207|              </tbody>
208|            </table>
209|          </div>
210|        </div>
211|      </section>
212|
213|      <ReviewHowItWorks />
214|
215|      <section class="engagement section-light" aria-labelledby="engagement-title">
216|        <div class="wrap">
217|          <p class="eyebrow dark">How engagements work</p>
218|          <h2 id="engagement-title">A complete marketing operation, without building one in-house.</h2>
219|          <div class="engagement-grid">
220|            <article><h3>Scoped to your business</h3><p>A monthly plan around the channels and volume you need, agreed before anything starts.</p></article>
221|            <article><h3>One connected scope</h3><p>Strategy, production, publishing, leads, and follow-up as one operation, defined by your plan.</p></article>
222|            <article><h3>Straightforward terms</h3><p>[No setup fee. No long contract. Pause and cancellation policy. Every term here publishes only once confirmed against actual operating terms.]</p></article>
223|          </div>
224|          <p class="investment">Markethink is built for businesses ready to invest consistently in their growth. For comparison, agencies delivering this work typically charge $3,000 to $15,000 a month.</p>
225|          <p>Plans are scoped per business, so a generic number would mislead in both directions. You will have your exact number after one 30-minute walkthrough, before any commitment. One conversation, one quote.</p>
226|        </div>
227|      </section>
228|
229|      <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
230|        <div class="wrap faq-grid">
231|          <div class="faq-heading">
232|            <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
233|            <h2 id="faq-title">The questions owners actually ask</h2>
234|          </div>
235|          <div class="accordions">
236|            {faq.map(([question, answer], index) => (
237|              <details open={index === 0}>
238|                <summary>{question}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
239|                <p>{answer}</p>
240|              </details>
241|            ))}
242|          </div>
243|        </div>
244|      </section>
245|
246|      <section class="final-cta section-light" id="preview-form" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
247|        <div class="wrap">
248|          <div class="cta-grid">
249|            <div>
250|              <p class="eyebrow dark">Campaign preview</p>
251|              <h2 id="cta-title">See what Markethink would ship for you.</h2>
252|              <p>Send us your website or Instagram. You get a private campaign preview: one campaign angle, one finished creative in your voice, one landing-page concept, and three prioritized opportunities. Nothing is published. Keep it either way.</p>
253|              <div class="preview-form" role="group" aria-label="Campaign preview request fields">
254|                <label>Website or Instagram<input type="url" placeholder="https://" /></label>
255|                <label>Email or WhatsApp<input type="text" /></label>
256|                <label>What does your business sell, in one sentence?<textarea rows="3"></textarea></label>
257|                <fieldset><legend>What monthly investment range are you considering for a managed marketing operation?</legend><label><input type="radio" name="budget" /> $500 to $1,000</label><label><input type="radio" name="budget" /> $1,000 to $2,000</label><label><input type="radio" name="budget" /> $2,000+</label></fieldset>
258|                <button class="button" type="button">Send me my campaign preview</button>
259|                <small>Built from your public brand only. Delivered privately by email or WhatsApp. Nothing is published.[Deletion promise only once a real retention and deletion process exists.]</small>
260|              </div>
261|            </div>
262|            <aside class="founder-call">
263|              <h3>Or talk to the founder directly.</h3>
264|              <p>A 30-minute call with Santiago Sosa. We bring your campaign preview, and you leave with your exact number.</p>
265|              <a class="button" href="/schedule-a-walkthrough/">Book a call with the founder</a>
266|              <div class="calendar-placeholder">
267|                <p>[COMPONENT] The booking calendar embeds inline right here, real availability visible, next to Santiago's photo. The qualifying questions (name, website, priority) are asked as booking fields, so booking is one step. This is the page's only inline calendar; everywhere else the walkthrough is a button.</p>
268|              </div>
269|            </aside>
270|          </div>
271|          <p class="proof-echo">[Proof echo beside the final CTA: the logo row repeated small, or the named result as one line.] Trust signals belong next to the moment of commitment, not only at the top.</p>
272|        </div>
273|      </section>
274|    </main>
